From edf33c38b301699167cc78cd4a465b03ed7df8c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Evolution BR811 <344454957+Evolution-BR811@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:47:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VGM/NSF import: shared instruments across channels, 04xy
 vibrato

- an instrument can serve every channel of the same chip (pulse,
  triangle, noise; SN squares and noise) when it sounds the same there
  (the duty is ignored on the triangle)
- copies whose arpeggio or pitch is the same moved by a constant amount
  become the same instrument: the note (or its E5xx) takes the difference
- vibratos that Furnace's 04xy makes exactly (songs made in Furnace) go
  to the pattern instead of a pitch macro; 0400 stops them, and the loop
  row sets the vibrato again

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KMJUrc1fn7dir5w2PfSPK2
---
 src/engine/fileOps/vgm.cpp | 203 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 190 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

